# RealtimeSanitizer suppressions for anira's CI (RTSAN_OPTIONS=suppressions=...).
#
# One known pre-existing violation class is suppressed so the job can gate
# everything else: anira's logging streams (LOG_ERROR/LOG_WARNING -> std::cerr/
# std::cout) flush from real-time paths in rare fallback branches, e.g. the
# "No free inference queue found" warning in Context::new_data_submitted. The
# fix (no logging from the audio thread) is tracked separately; suppressing by
# the ostream frames keeps the scope exactly "logging via streams" —
# allocations, locks, sleeps, and semaphore syscalls on real-time paths still
# abort the job. (The buffers are tanh-lib's logger-free containers: a ring
# overflow overwrites silently, so no suppression is needed for them.)
call-stack-contains:basic_ostream
